From d5fe0af0158cbcac7708f653fe44b7df8c967162 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Quintin Smits <qd.smits@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 23:29:45 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/6] feat(gcode): the Klartext reader reads RND, CHF and polar
 LP / CP

Third slice of the HEIDENHAIN Klartext reader:
- RND (rounding arc) and CHF (chamfer) between two straight feed lines
  (L or LP) in the working plane, by one-block look-ahead: the line
  before waits, the line after sets the cut-back points. The F of the
  transition acts only on it.
- LP with PR/PA and IPR/IPA about the pole CC.
- CP with PA or IPA and DR, with Z/IZ as a helix, split into pieces of
  at most 90 degrees.
Transitions next to arcs, FMAX lines, Z changes or block-end M
functions, a CP IPA/DR sign mismatch and polar angles at the pole are
refused by name and line. RL/RR, APPR/DEP, CTP, LBL and inch programs
stay refused.

Refs #2227

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
