From 55386f6bd408d62051526460a039b4c2bbfc5e61 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Quintin Smits <qd.smits@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 01:36:51 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 5/6] fix(gcode): Klartext LP refuses an unknown last polar
 coordinate; no zero-length transition line

- LP: a polar coordinate that is not written, and the base of IPR / IPA,
  is the last programmed PR / PA about the current pole. The reader keeps
  it only while it knows it exactly (an LP or CP about the same pole, no
  X/Y move by another block, no moved CC). Else the LP is refused by name
  and line ("LP without PR: the last polar radius about this pole is not
  known"). Same rule for PA.
- RND / CHF that takes exactly the whole line writes no zero-length feed
  move for that line.
- New tests: polar reference refusals and keeps, LP angle out of range,
  whole-line transitions, RND after M3/M8, CHF with an LP line, FMAX on a
  transition.

Refs #2227

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
